A4.26 · Save the training card on the position after White's move. If a card already exists, only its target move and its explanation text are updated — the review schedule is left alone. If not, create it: due now, never reviewed, with its starting difficulty. The explanation text holds the score, human-data volume, and displayed evaluation. ^W0Qb7iPd

A4.08 searches by the full FEN, but nodes made by the current code store a shortened FEN without the two move counters. A4.08 therefore never finds one, so A4.09’s “yes” route never runs. If the exact move history already exists, A4.10 tries to create a duplicate node and the run stops at A4.10.

A4.14’s “yes” route is also unreachable during normal single-run operation for a separate reason: a found node with a training card would already have left through A4.09’s “yes” route. A node that reaches A4.14 therefore has no card. ^bCi20EGa

